<table border="0" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" width="100%"><tr><td>
<a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=20"><img src="images/topics/live.gif" border="0" Alt="Live" align="right" hspace="10" vspace="10"></a>
<div align=justify><font class="posted" color="#000000"><P><STRONG>The Church Maná is&nbsp; trying to&nbsp;reach an agreement&nbsp; with John Giddings, Madonna's lawyer,&nbsp;regarding the Convention of Faith and the concert from the singer, both&nbsp;slated for September&nbsp; in the Atlantic Pavilion, in Lisbon.&nbsp; </STRONG></P>
<P>Tânia Tadeu, from the Church Maná, revealed to the<STRONG> Lusa</STRONG> that, after<STRONG> John Giddings</STRONG> met <STRONG>Jorge Tadeu, president from the Church</STRONG>, an agreement will be settled, "although, being The&nbsp;Convention&nbsp; an international event and&nbsp;Tv&nbsp;show, it will be no easy to change its date".&nbsp; </P>
<P><STRONG>Ricardo Casimiro, the promoter of&nbsp;Madonna's concert&nbsp; in Portugal, is accused of&nbsp; instigation among the &nbsp;fans&nbsp;of &nbsp;the artist</STRONG> <STRONG>against the Church</STRONG>.</P>
<P>The origin of the misunderstanding is the fact ,that &nbsp;<STRONG>in February,&nbsp; Maná Christian Church&nbsp; requested the Atlantic Pavilion</STRONG> for&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;its&nbsp;<STRONG>yearly Convention&nbsp;of the Faith&nbsp;from 08 to 11 of September</STRONG>, while the Atlantic was requested ,<STRONG> in April,&nbsp;from 09 to 13 of the same month,&nbsp;to be used for Madonna's concert&nbsp; </STRONG></P>
<P>The Church Maná - that has&nbsp;fixed for the next week a&nbsp;press conference&nbsp; with John Giddings,the "new official representative Portuguese" for the singer, an element from the Church Maná and another for the Atlantic Pavilion -&nbsp;pointed that it<STRONG>&nbsp;"has nothing against Madonna" and that this is not "a battle of the&nbsp;Good against the Evil".&nbsp; </STRONG></P>
<P>&nbsp;</P>
<P>&nbsp;</P>
</font></div>
</td></tr></table>


