<table border="0" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" width="100%"><tr><td>
<a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=20"><img src="images/topics/live.gif" border="0" Alt="Live" align="right" hspace="10" vspace="10"></a>
<div align=justify><font class="posted" color="#000000"><P>Madonna<BR><BR>By David Pencek<BR><B>Norwich Bulletin </B><BR>Nearly every pop star today --<B> from Britney Spears to Christina Aguilera -- mentions the same person as their hero. Madonna. </B><BR>The 45-year-old Madonna isn't about to let all the new starlets have all the fun this summer. <B>She is on her "Reinvention Tour" that visits Worcester's Centrum Centre for not one, not two, not three -- but, four shows. </B><BR>In her only New England appearance, Madonna begins her four-night stay at the Centrum Centre Sunday. She follows that with performances Monday, Wednesday and July 1. <BR><BR><B>The shows begin at 8 p.m. and are sold out, except for the July 1 concert. <BR><BR>Tickets are $45-$300. </B><BR>Madonna's concert "blends elements of Broadway, Cirque du Soleil, Rock the Vote rallies, art installations, extreme sporting events, church sermons, disco dances and gun-spinning military drills," according to a Washington Post review of her show earlier this month at the MCI Center. <BR><BR>Unlike her 2001 "Drowned World Tour," Madonna performs more of her past hits, such as "Papa Don't Preach" and "Into The Groove." She also performs songs from her 2003 album, "American Life," which sold poorly. <BR><BR>Last week, Madonna finally settled her dispute with Warner Music Group by selling her share of Maverick Records to its joint venture partner. The deal gives Warner nearly 80 percent ownership of Maverick. Madonna was a co-founder of Maverick and the label includes artists such as Alanis Morissette and Michelle Branch. <BR><BR>Ticket information: Go online to www.centrumcentre.com or call 617-228-6000</P>
<P><IMG src="http://www.drownedmadonna.com/re/Worcester_Centrum_small.jpg" border=0><BR></P>
</font></div>
</td></tr></table>


</td></tr></table>


