<table border="0" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" width="100%"><tr><td>
<a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=10"><img src="images/topics/photos.gif" border="0" Alt="Photos" align="right" hspace="10" vspace="10"></a>
<div align=justify><font class="posted" color="#000000"><P><STRONG>The Sun </STRONG>seems to confirm <STRONG>The exclusive</STRONG> brought to you yesterday by <STRONG>SexedUpCity</STRONG> on<STRONG> </STRONG><A href="www.drownedmadonna.com"><STRONG>Drownedmadonna</STRONG></A>: <STRONG>Guy Ritchie</STRONG> is working on a&nbsp; new <STRONG>commercial</STRONG> for a red Corvette!</P>
<P>Here's what <STRONG>Sun</STRONG> writes Today:</P>
<P><SPAN class=norm12>DON’T be too surprised if little <STRONG>ROCCO RITCHIE</STRONG> follows in his director dad’s film-making footsteps. </P>
<P>The little nipper got some behind-the-camera experience on the set of his dad <STRONG>GUY</STRONG>’s latest filming job – and looked like he loved every minute.</P>
<P><STRONG>MADONNA</STRONG> brought the couple’s son and her daughter <STRONG>LOURDES</STRONG> to the set of the Corvette car ad in New York on Fathers’ Day. The youngsters charmed the crew by playing with traffic cones.</P>
<P>And Guy, who made Brit classics Lock, Stock &amp; Two Smoking Barrels and Snatch, impressed the family with a two-hour filming masterclass.</P>
<P>A film set insider said: “Little Rocco was fascinated by his father’s every move.”</P>
<P><STRONG>Watch the exclusive pics by clicking <A href="http://www.thesun.co.uk/article/0,,4-2004290891,00.html">here</A></STRONG></P>
<P>&nbsp;</P>
<P><BR>&nbsp;</P></SPAN>
<P>&nbsp;</P>
</font></div>
</td></tr></table>


